WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.938
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.208 --> 00:06.209
[Previously…]

3
00:06.338 --> 00:07.920
We usually leave girls alone.

4
00:08.056 --> 00:09.560
But when it comes to the Monchaitrakuls,

5
00:09.773 --> 00:12.060
no one's getting spared. Not even women or children.

6
00:12.120 --> 00:13.960
Someone actually died

7
00:13.997 --> 00:16.160
because of the feud between our two families,

8
00:16.600 --> 00:18.800
Uncle Wirat, Pakkard's father.

9
00:19.147 --> 00:21.360
You have to cut ties with that family.

10
00:21.899 --> 00:25.000
I understand if you don't want to be with me.

11
00:25.100 --> 00:28.440
They made this mess. Let them deal with it.

12
00:49.811 --> 00:51.012
If I’d gotten there in time that day,

13
00:51.859 --> 00:53.120
your father might still be alive.

14
00:54.040 --> 00:55.240
Did you know beforehand

15
00:56.214 --> 00:57.360
that something was going to happen?

16
00:58.934 --> 01:00.000
I know those people well.

17
01:01.110 --> 01:03.680
They may act generous toward the villagers,

18
01:04.358 --> 01:07.520
but they’ve always played dirty.

19
01:12.382 --> 01:14.200
But we don’t have any proof.

20
01:15.179 --> 01:18.560
I think some things should be left in the past.

21
01:20.784 --> 01:24.285
Then leave this matter to the adults.

22
02:38.680 --> 02:39.681
ANNA SIRIN KONGPURIM

23
02:39.704 --> 02:41.400
Mom would be so happy if she could see this.

24
02:42.600 --> 02:43.601
You know

25
02:44.931 --> 02:47.080
how much she loved white roses, don’t you?

26
02:50.915 --> 02:52.440
How would she know, Dad?

27
02:53.896 --> 02:55.680
She’s never even seen Mom’s face in person.

28
02:57.011 --> 02:58.780
But she looks exactly like Mom.

29
02:59.760 --> 03:01.161
All she has to do is look in the mirror.

30
03:03.161 --> 03:04.162
Isn’t that right, sweetheart?

31
03:08.184 --> 03:09.640
The saddest day of my life

32
03:10.320 --> 03:12.760
was the day I couldn’t protect your mother

33
03:13.614 --> 03:14.980
when the accident happened.

34
03:17.582 --> 03:19.640
I won’t let anything like that happen again.

35
03:23.920 --> 03:25.621
As long as I can keep an eye on you,

36
03:27.355 --> 03:28.520
I won’t have anything to worry about.

37
03:36.723 --> 03:37.724
Tokyo.

38
03:40.232 --> 03:42.600
You’re not involved with that family’s daughter, are you?

39
03:49.051 --> 03:50.480
What do you mean, Dad?

40
03:51.548 --> 03:52.600
Exactly what I said.

41
03:54.417 --> 03:57.160
Seeing her, talking to her,

42
03:57.660 --> 03:58.661
or being friends with her.

43
03:59.966 --> 04:01.730
You’re not doing any of that, are you?

44
04:14.080 --> 04:15.780
We’re just in the same class. That’s all.

45
04:21.090 --> 04:23.130
I don’t want to have to watch my back around outsiders

46
04:24.430 --> 04:26.600
and then be suspicious of my own family too.

47
04:29.960 --> 04:31.040
If you promise me,

48
04:33.200 --> 04:34.401
I’ll trust you.

49
04:39.070 --> 04:40.071
I promise.

50
04:42.798 --> 04:44.280
I won’t let you down, Dad.

51
05:29.254 --> 05:30.255
Boss.

52
05:31.019 --> 05:33.040
The situation at our port still hasn’t settled down.

53
05:33.835 --> 05:34.836
The other night,

54
05:35.275 --> 05:38.240
people were still sneaking in and causing trouble.

55
05:39.131 --> 05:42.132
And that’s not even counting those spreading rumors

56
05:43.000 --> 05:44.480
to frighten the villagers.

57
05:44.533 --> 05:46.720
The community leaders have been resigning one after another.

58
05:47.896 --> 05:48.897
What should we do, Boss?

59
05:51.278 --> 05:52.840
Throw money at the problem for now.

60
05:53.907 --> 05:55.480
Whatever they want, pay them.

61
05:56.414 --> 05:59.720
Right now, we need as many villagers on our side as possible.

62
06:00.440 --> 06:01.441
Yes, Boss.

63
06:05.326 --> 06:06.360
And what about Blue?

64
06:09.064 --> 06:11.600
I’m not letting that matter go.

65
06:55.264 --> 06:58.040
Dude, is that a real kiss or just the camera angle?

66
07:03.030 --> 07:05.080
Why are you zooming in so much?

67
07:05.180 --> 07:06.681
Zooming in won’t change anything.

68
07:06.690 --> 07:07.880
I told you, I saw it with my own eyes.

69
07:08.990 --> 07:11.480
What do we do? Should we tell Yi?

70
07:11.795 --> 07:12.796
Damn it.

71
07:13.614 --> 07:15.440
Why the hell did they have to get together?

72
07:15.790 --> 07:17.291
Don’t their families hate each other?

73
07:18.040 --> 07:20.180
What, are they trying to be Romeo and Juliet?

74
07:21.214 --> 07:23.180
So what are we doing? Are we telling Yi or not?

75
07:23.230 --> 07:25.280
How the hell should I know?

76
07:27.566 --> 07:28.567
Here.

77
07:29.838 --> 07:30.939
And this pile too.

78
07:31.555 --> 07:33.460
Put them in the right shelves, okay?

79
07:56.960 --> 07:58.320
My dad’s getting suspicious.

80
07:58.850 --> 08:00.760
We’ll have to be more careful for a while.

81
08:02.080 --> 08:03.081
Okay.

82
08:21.211 --> 08:22.560
- I should go. - Okay.

83
08:29.323 --> 08:30.324
Come on. Let’s go.

84
08:42.491 --> 08:44.251
Chanthara Suksa has sent us

85
08:44.310 --> 08:47.880
its list of representatives for this year’s friendship event.

86
08:47.947 --> 08:50.168
As for Chantrarawatthana,

87
08:50.182 --> 08:53.280
I’ve put Tokyo’s name down, Principal.

88
08:53.536 --> 08:55.680
How much did he contribute last year?

89
08:56.358 --> 08:58.880
They provided a budget of two million baht.

90
09:00.144 --> 09:02.000
Then let’s ask for a little more this year.

91
09:02.640 --> 09:04.880
Tokyo is already in Grade 12.

92
09:06.067 --> 09:08.400
If the event isn’t grand enough to live up to the Kongpurim name,

93
09:09.190 --> 09:10.680
I don’t think that would look good.

94
09:11.718 --> 09:13.960
Can Mr. Po still afford it, Principal?

95
09:14.176 --> 09:16.920
He’s been strapped for cash since he lost the port concession.

96
09:17.077 --> 09:20.278
His men have been collecting interest from the local vendors more aggressively than ever.

97
09:21.235 --> 09:22.520
Does that include you?

98
09:23.374 --> 09:25.480
Yes, but I’m not the only one.

99
09:25.520 --> 09:28.521
Some teachers can’t keep up with their teachers’ cooperative loan payments either.

100
09:28.580 --> 09:31.430
Mr. Po has tightened his purse strings and stopped lending them money to stay afloat.

101
09:32.581 --> 09:35.699
Then why don’t we put Phakjira in charge of the students

102
09:35.710 --> 09:37.699
for this event instead?

103
09:38.056 --> 09:42.357
After all, her father is about to replace Mr. Po.

104
09:42.592 --> 09:44.788
He should be able to support our budget.

105
09:45.131 --> 09:48.080
But will Mr. Wiboon be as generous as Mr. Po?

106
09:48.822 --> 09:51.080
There’s no harm in trying.

107
09:51.153 --> 09:55.000
After all, the one person we know is short on cash is Mr. Po.

108
09:56.154 --> 09:57.555
[ School Principal ]

109
09:57.780 --> 09:59.880
All right. Here’s what we’ll do.

110
10:03.091 --> 10:04.092
What?

111
10:04.446 --> 10:05.960
Why does it have to be me again?

112
10:06.995 --> 10:09.320
You already made me do the bulletin board last time.

113
10:10.780 --> 10:13.580
It’s not just you. I’ve assigned Tokyo too.

114
10:14.550 --> 10:16.200
You’ll be working as a pair.

115
10:16.760 --> 10:18.461
I’m not asking you to do it alone.

116
10:28.582 --> 10:29.640
What do you think we should do?

117
10:31.195 --> 10:32.240
Hmm.

118
10:33.243 --> 10:34.680
There are so many details.

119
10:36.526 --> 10:39.000
Can we finish it in time with so few people?

120
10:43.624 --> 10:46.320
And this is the friendship event.

121
10:46.504 --> 10:47.840
Are these really all the people who came to help?

122
10:51.912 --> 10:53.840
Who wants to work for free?

123
10:55.496 --> 10:57.840
They’re probably off flirting with boys from other schools.

124
11:02.094 --> 11:05.240
Then let’s hurry up and get this done.

125
11:07.587 --> 11:09.880
Blue, I’m sorry, but...

126
11:10.184 --> 11:12.330
if we finish helping today,

127
11:12.480 --> 11:14.481
could you ask your father

128
11:14.491 --> 11:16.280
to let my dad work at the port again?

129
11:17.358 --> 11:18.379
And for me,

130
11:18.558 --> 11:20.800
could you talk to the teacher who gave me an Incomplete?

131
11:23.640 --> 11:25.755
Wait. What exactly does everyone think

132
11:25.915 --> 11:27.240
I can help you with?

133
11:27.440 --> 11:30.600
Doesn’t your father run the port?

134
11:30.891 --> 11:33.440
If we can’t ask you for help, who else can we ask?

135
11:34.250 --> 11:36.480
Can’t you even do this much for your friends?

136
11:40.640 --> 11:42.000
I can’t help any of you.

137
11:42.667 --> 11:45.000
I came here today to design the Moon Night stage.

138
11:46.720 --> 11:48.400
If you came expecting anything else, just leave.

139
11:53.976 --> 11:54.977
What?

140
12:04.363 --> 12:05.364
It’s okay.

141
12:06.164 --> 12:07.440
I’ll lend a hand too.

142
12:09.365 --> 12:13.320
With this few people, we’ll only have a wooden frame by the day of the event.

143
12:24.531 --> 12:26.360
What are we going to do?

144
12:27.080 --> 12:28.600
Why don’t you let us help?

145
12:30.560 --> 12:31.720
What? Why are you scooting away?

146
12:32.387 --> 12:35.240
Why are you squeezing in with us? Just stay where you were.

147
12:41.022 --> 12:43.200
Come on. Everyone knows about you two already.

148
12:43.294 --> 12:46.120
Yeah. You’re the only one who never thought to tell your friends.

149
12:46.323 --> 12:47.324
Yeah.

150
12:48.350 --> 12:49.520
You two already knew?

151
12:54.899 --> 12:55.900
Go on.

152
12:57.283 --> 12:58.284
I’m sorry.

153
12:59.939 --> 13:02.120
I just didn’t know how to bring it up.

154
13:02.566 --> 13:04.310
You could’ve just told us.

155
13:04.800 --> 13:05.801
Exactly.

156
13:13.363 --> 13:16.643
But you know what my family is like.

157
13:16.675 --> 13:19.400
Yeah, I know. I know everything.

158
13:19.587 --> 13:21.760
Yi told the two of us

159
13:21.800 --> 13:23.520
to keep an eye on you and Blue.

160
13:23.923 --> 13:26.878
Yi even used our parents to threaten us.

161
13:27.267 --> 13:28.268
That's right.

162
13:29.704 --> 13:31.280
Don’t look at me like that.

163
13:31.380 --> 13:33.840
I’ve applied for a part-time job in case I need to help my parents.

164
13:34.184 --> 13:36.380
And in case Yi ever comes to collect the debt,

165
13:36.440 --> 13:37.541
we’d be screwed. What else was I supposed to do?

166
13:38.667 --> 13:40.224
Exactly. And one more thing.

167
13:40.246 --> 13:42.360
We’re not friends with you because of your money,

168
13:42.380 --> 13:43.792
no matter what everyone else says.

169
13:49.528 --> 13:50.720
Oh my goodness.

170
13:57.694 --> 13:58.800
Thank you.

171
14:01.165 --> 14:02.166
Not so fast.

172
14:02.310 --> 14:04.440
Don’t tell Yi

173
14:04.560 --> 14:05.800
that we already know.

174
14:06.480 --> 14:07.481
Keep it quiet.

175
14:09.552 --> 14:10.553
Okay, okay.

176
14:27.190 --> 14:28.360
Give them a hug too.

177
14:44.136 --> 14:45.518
Oh, perfect timing.

178
14:46.430 --> 14:48.240
Come here, sweetheart. Come on.

179
14:57.304 --> 14:58.305
Here she is.

180
15:01.998 --> 15:04.200
You said you wanted to study in London, right?

181
15:04.643 --> 15:06.640
So I hired a tutor to give you a trial lesson.

182
15:12.360 --> 15:13.361
Yes,

183
15:13.920 --> 15:16.230
but what I meant was that I wanted to study in London.

184
15:17.360 --> 15:19.261
Just try it and see if you like it.

185
15:19.686 --> 15:21.080
If you really do,

186
15:21.243 --> 15:23.880
I’ll hire someone to design a whole curriculum and teach you right here.

187
15:24.510 --> 15:26.240
That way, you won’t have to go so far away.

188
15:31.038 --> 15:32.760
Come, have a seat.

189
15:33.560 --> 15:34.561
You should talk to her.

190
15:39.160 --> 15:41.000
Please take good care of my daughter.

191
15:41.376 --> 15:42.377
Of course.

192
15:46.766 --> 15:49.886
Should we start by getting to know each other better?

193
15:51.646 --> 15:52.647
Okay.

194
15:53.224 --> 15:55.180
Which literary works do you like most?

195
15:59.195 --> 16:00.360
Romeo & Juliet.

196
16:02.080 --> 16:03.166
Great choice.

197
16:04.440 --> 16:06.200
What about Hamlet?

198
16:09.182 --> 16:10.480
I've read all of this.

199
16:17.696 --> 16:19.800
Is that enough to step outside

200
16:20.571 --> 16:22.180
and learn from the real world?

201
16:24.174 --> 16:25.720
With a strong purpose in your heart,

202
16:26.520 --> 16:27.960
you can find out who you want to be

203
16:28.440 --> 16:29.441
wherever you are.

204
16:39.710 --> 16:41.120
What's wrong?

205
16:59.190 --> 17:01.960
Whoa, you’re a pretty good shot.

206
17:02.880 --> 17:03.881
That’s because I had a good teacher.

207
17:04.330 --> 17:07.070
True. A good teacher—and handsome too.

208
17:08.952 --> 17:11.400
You just got a new gun. Why don't you try your old one?

209
17:12.451 --> 17:13.699
- You think? - Yeah.

210
17:23.144 --> 17:24.145
You're right.

211
17:25.160 --> 17:26.920
Then you can have my new one. I don’t want it anymore.

212
17:28.787 --> 17:30.480
What would I even use it for?

213
17:31.427 --> 17:33.200
I don’t want to grow up to be like you.

214
17:33.228 --> 17:35.680
Wow. Listen to you.

215
17:40.187 --> 17:41.420
- Yi. - Yeah?

216
17:41.830 --> 17:42.880
I’m seriously asking.

217
17:44.544 --> 17:46.330
Have you ever wanted to try doing something else?

218
17:47.536 --> 17:49.120
Something that doesn’t involve working for Dad?

219
17:51.512 --> 17:52.513
No, never.

220
17:54.942 --> 17:55.960
But I do.

221
18:00.080 --> 18:01.600
Then do whatever you want.

222
18:01.696 --> 18:02.697
Dad won’t stop you.

223
18:03.560 --> 18:05.040
But do you really have to leave home?

224
18:07.040 --> 18:08.181
If I never leave,

225
18:08.190 --> 18:10.064
how will I find out what I truly enjoy?

226
18:10.130 --> 18:12.040
How will I discover my dream or what I want to do?

227
18:12.331 --> 18:13.332
I have to leave.

228
18:14.202 --> 18:15.480
I’ve never had to leave home,

229
18:15.503 --> 18:17.240
but I still know what I want and what I enjoy.

230
18:19.220 --> 18:20.560
But you didn’t choose any of it yourself.

231
18:20.984 --> 18:22.040
Dad chose it for you.

232
18:25.704 --> 18:27.705
Shooting. Boxing.

233
18:28.035 --> 18:30.080
Running gambling dens. Collecting debts.

234
18:31.704 --> 18:33.705
Did Dad ever ask if you wanted to do any of that?

235
18:35.320 --> 18:36.321
No.

236
18:37.331 --> 18:39.040
Maybe Dad made you do those things for so long

237
18:39.224 --> 18:40.840
that you convinced yourself you liked them.

238
18:43.480 --> 18:45.181
But I think I really do like them.

239
18:45.681 --> 18:46.720
I honestly feel

240
18:47.214 --> 18:48.960
like I was born for this.

241
18:52.472 --> 18:53.800
Then you’re lucky.

242
18:55.469 --> 18:58.280
You didn’t choose it, but you still ended up liking it.

243
18:59.080 --> 19:00.081
Okay.

244
19:00.494 --> 19:01.580
But for me,

245
19:02.606 --> 19:03.920
I don’t think this life is for me.

246
19:05.880 --> 19:07.096
I think I need to choose for myself.

247
19:07.966 --> 19:08.967
I don’t want this.

248
19:11.272 --> 19:12.800
Do you really want to go abroad that badly?

249
19:23.846 --> 19:24.847
Fine.

250
19:25.312 --> 19:26.400
I’ll talk to Dad for you.

251
19:27.755 --> 19:29.005
- You will? - Yeah.

252
19:30.000 --> 19:31.920
Make sure you find out what your dream is.

253
19:32.598 --> 19:34.240
- Really? - Sure.

254
19:51.179 --> 19:52.320
You're healed now.

255
19:57.928 --> 20:00.238
Hey, tell me something.

256
20:00.920 --> 20:02.400
How did you figure out what your dream was?

257
20:04.040 --> 20:05.880
What made you ask me that?

258
20:08.710 --> 20:10.560
I want to have a dream like you do.

259
20:12.451 --> 20:14.760
Have you loved drawing since you were little?

260
20:21.078 --> 20:22.730
It was a long time ago. You’re better off not knowing.

261
20:24.155 --> 20:26.840
Why? Can’t you tell me?

262
20:27.451 --> 20:28.800
Please tell me.

263
20:29.328 --> 20:30.329
Please?

264
20:31.180 --> 20:32.880
Come on, please.

265
20:35.240 --> 20:36.241
Please?

266
20:37.072 --> 20:38.160
It was because of Tong.

267
20:49.318 --> 20:50.440
Your ex?

268
20:52.368 --> 20:53.369
Yeah.

269
20:54.630 --> 20:56.200
Tong invited me to take art lessons.

270
21:01.440 --> 21:04.582
See? This is why I didn’t want to tell you.

271
21:06.670 --> 21:08.283
You once told me

272
21:08.659 --> 21:10.840
that your father had chosen a path for each of his children.

273
21:12.660 --> 21:13.800
What did he choose for you?

274
21:19.800 --> 21:20.801
I don’t know either.

275
21:22.150 --> 21:23.320
Dad’s never told me.

276
21:26.600 --> 21:28.580
It’s different with Yi and Big.

277
21:30.080 --> 21:33.630
Dad had Yi learn the family business from a young age.

278
21:34.640 --> 21:35.720
As for Big,

279
21:36.782 --> 21:38.283
Dad had him train to become a police officer

280
21:38.880 --> 21:40.881
so he could handle things whenever there was trouble.

281
21:44.472 --> 21:45.473
But as for me,

282
21:51.982 --> 21:54.480
maybe Dad doesn’t think I have any special talents.

283
21:56.683 --> 21:59.560
That’s a good thing. It means you get to choose for yourself.

284
22:04.438 --> 22:05.439
I may get to choose,

285
22:05.851 --> 22:08.000
but that doesn’t mean things will work out.

286
22:17.630 --> 22:18.631
Just hypothetically...

287
22:19.795 --> 22:21.440
what if we couldn’t be together in person?

288
22:22.920 --> 22:25.121
What if I stayed here

289
22:26.304 --> 22:28.120
while you went to study in Bangkok?

290
22:30.011 --> 22:31.012
Do you think...

291
22:32.112 --> 22:33.480
we’d still be together?

292
22:34.486 --> 22:37.080
Even if we had to live apart

293
22:37.995 --> 22:40.000
and have a long-distance relationship instead?

294
22:41.952 --> 22:43.440
Do we really have to break up?

295
22:44.200 --> 22:45.720
I don’t want to do long-distance.

296
22:54.112 --> 22:55.440
But I was only speaking hypothetically.

297
22:56.059 --> 22:58.241
No matter what, I’m going with you.

298
22:59.060 --> 23:00.760
I’ll just close my eyes and pick a program.

299
23:01.040 --> 23:03.320
There must be one I can get into with my scores.

300
23:05.851 --> 23:06.852
Please don't.

301
23:10.286 --> 23:13.240
I don’t want you choosing your dream because of me.

302
23:15.048 --> 23:16.440
If you rush into making a choice

303
23:17.416 --> 23:19.080
and regret it later,

304
23:19.982 --> 23:21.880
you might end up resenting me for it.

305
23:25.539 --> 23:27.930
I want you to choose for yourself.

306
23:28.446 --> 23:30.640
But the problem is, I don’t have any other dreams.

307
23:35.064 --> 23:36.680
You’re my dream.

308
23:51.200 --> 23:54.201
[Singing off-key.]

309
24:03.672 --> 24:05.020
Everyone.

310
24:06.403 --> 24:09.480
Today, a representative from Chanthara Suksa

311
24:09.504 --> 24:11.120
will be joining our rehearsal.

312
24:11.360 --> 24:13.323
Our opening performance

313
24:13.371 --> 24:15.120
will feature both bands performing together.

314
24:16.224 --> 24:17.670
Oh, perfect timing.

315
24:17.904 --> 24:18.905
Come on over.

316
24:30.312 --> 24:31.440
Everyone, this is Tong.

317
24:31.566 --> 24:33.440
Stand here so everyone can see you clearly.

318
24:33.790 --> 24:36.800
Tong Nattapong is representing Chanthara Suksa.

319
24:36.899 --> 24:38.530
Why don’t you all get to know one another?

320
24:39.152 --> 24:40.800
Please make him feel welcome.

321
24:43.683 --> 24:46.560
Let’s work on the sets and props outside today.

322
24:47.235 --> 24:49.180
That way, we won’t disturb the band’s rehearsal.

323
24:57.211 --> 24:58.390
Oh, hi.

324
24:58.939 --> 25:00.380
- Hello. - Tong, right?

325
25:00.470 --> 25:02.600
- Yeah. - I'm Jai, I'm the leader of the school band.

326
25:02.683 --> 25:03.684
I'm also a lead singer.

327
25:04.140 --> 25:05.392
Oh, you were great earlier.

328
25:05.509 --> 25:06.510
Tong.

329
25:06.680 --> 25:09.200
Why don’t you rehearse with the band’s backup vocalists?

330
25:10.080 --> 25:11.280
What do you mean, ma’am?

331
25:11.971 --> 25:14.040
Jiwara, why are you still sitting there? Come on.

332
25:14.099 --> 25:15.100
Come rehearse.

333
25:17.100 --> 25:18.240
Here’s the thing.

334
25:18.854 --> 25:21.520
The principal considers this a major event,

335
25:21.555 --> 25:23.356
and the school’s reputation is at stake.

336
25:23.552 --> 25:25.640
You’re not suitable to be the lead singer for this event.

337
25:25.910 --> 25:28.000
But you can’t do this, ma’am.

338
25:28.211 --> 25:30.000
I’ve been rehearsing for this event all year.

339
25:30.012 --> 25:31.880
You can’t just replace me whenever you feel like it.

340
25:32.006 --> 25:33.800
You need to accept the truth, Sophawan.

341
25:33.926 --> 25:36.600
You were never suited to be the school’s lead singer.

342
25:36.930 --> 25:38.960
You should know how you got that position in the first place.

343
25:40.000 --> 25:41.920
- I'll be right back. - Okay.

344
25:49.219 --> 25:50.220
Blue.

345
25:50.483 --> 25:51.939
Blue!

346
25:53.912 --> 25:55.000
Why the hell did you do that?

347
25:55.726 --> 25:57.760
What? Long time no see.

348
25:57.918 --> 25:59.240
Aren’t you going to say hello properly?

349
25:59.430 --> 26:00.431
Are you trying to start something?

350
26:01.062 --> 26:02.720
Why did you have to follow me here?

351
26:03.622 --> 26:05.840
Well, you gave me the idea.

352
26:05.979 --> 26:07.640
I want a university admissions quota too.

353
26:08.838 --> 26:09.839
That’s ridiculous.

354
26:10.723 --> 26:12.780
You were already a school athlete back there.

355
26:13.616 --> 26:14.800
What quota could you possibly need here?

356
26:15.608 --> 26:17.009
Stop making excuses.

357
26:21.963 --> 26:22.964
The truth is...

358
26:24.166 --> 26:25.680
I want you to give me another chance.

359
26:27.494 --> 26:29.320
You said you didn’t like long-distance relationships, remember?

360
26:29.340 --> 26:30.800
Now I’ve moved closer to you.

361
26:31.870 --> 26:33.130
Can we start seeing each other again?

362
26:34.222 --> 26:36.440
Breaking up because of the distance wasn’t fair to me, Blue.

363
26:39.406 --> 26:40.407
Forget it.

364
26:41.607 --> 26:42.880
That second chance you want?

365
26:44.344 --> 26:45.400
I don’t have one to give you.

366
26:51.160 --> 26:52.480
Is it because you're dating someone?

367
26:57.355 --> 26:58.356
That has nothing to do with it.

368
26:59.872 --> 27:01.240
What’s over

369
27:02.254 --> 27:03.280
is over.

370
27:06.750 --> 27:07.761
I’m not giving up.

371
27:09.294 --> 27:10.440
I’ll show you

372
27:10.460 --> 27:12.040
that being with me is the better choice.

373
27:14.059 --> 27:15.060
Pretty confident, aren’t you?

374
27:31.427 --> 27:32.920
That was Tong, wasn’t it?

375
27:35.112 --> 27:36.113
Yeah.

376
27:37.424 --> 27:38.760
But I didn’t invite him here.

377
27:40.208 --> 27:41.280
He came on his own.

378
27:44.955 --> 27:45.956
I didn’t say you did.

379
27:47.227 --> 27:48.960
But once this event is over, you won’t be seeing him again, right?

380
27:49.718 --> 27:50.719
Right?

381
28:42.304 --> 28:43.800
I’d like Police Commander Sin

382
28:44.406 --> 28:47.120
to look after and protect me and my family,

383
28:48.240 --> 28:50.760
just as you would any other citizens in this province.

384
28:58.203 --> 28:59.204
What?

385
29:01.560 --> 29:02.680
The police got a tip about our gambling den.

386
29:03.240 --> 29:05.000
Police Commander Sin said we’ve been operating too openly.

387
29:05.424 --> 29:07.120
We have to shut it down for now. The police are raiding it tomorrow.

388
29:11.488 --> 29:13.040
If you’re this useless,

389
29:14.480 --> 29:17.993
why the hell did I pay all those bribes to get you into the police force?

390
29:21.416 --> 29:22.600
They’re coming down hard on us this time.

391
29:24.344 --> 29:26.400
They made a deal directly with Police Commander Sin.

392
29:29.837 --> 29:32.240
The influential officials who took side with the family that won the port concession,

393
29:32.280 --> 29:33.281
you should--

394
29:42.059 --> 29:45.200
What the fuck is Commander Sin playing at? That bastard!

395
29:47.640 --> 29:50.120
He told us to lay low with the gambling den and the underground lottery for now.

396
29:53.462 --> 29:54.463
More importantly,

397
29:57.270 --> 29:59.040
he ordered us to stay away from that family.

398
29:59.449 --> 30:02.040
That fucking Commander Sin talked to us like we were dirt.

399
30:02.760 --> 30:05.120
Does he plan on returning any of the money we paid him?

400
30:05.315 --> 30:06.920
We should be grateful he isn’t demanding even more.

401
30:07.528 --> 30:10.229
This is because you went after Wiboon’s daughter.

402
30:11.360 --> 30:12.961
You handed them an opening to attack us.

403
30:14.640 --> 30:15.880
Don’t you understand that we can’t shut down the gambling den

404
30:15.941 --> 30:17.360
and the underground lottery?

405
30:17.510 --> 30:19.511
I need that cash to keep our men on our side.

406
30:19.780 --> 30:21.680
What are you gonna do if all our men switch sides and join the Monchaitrakuls?

407
30:21.760 --> 30:23.680
I’ve told you not to buy your men’s loyalty with money.

408
30:23.720 --> 30:24.721
Do you ever listen to me?

409
30:24.870 --> 30:27.040
- Use your brain for once-- - Shhh.

410
30:27.320 --> 30:28.321
Enough.

411
30:34.120 --> 30:35.121
Hey,

412
30:45.720 --> 30:47.680
I'm gonna take this one.

413
30:57.915 --> 30:59.320
Come on.

414
30:59.800 --> 31:01.360
It's okay.

415
31:02.091 --> 31:04.040
It’s okay if you’re not the school’s lead singer.

416
31:04.760 --> 31:08.020
Honestly, it’s not that surprising.

417
31:08.440 --> 31:10.480
Anyone who’s heard you sing could’ve seen it coming.

418
31:11.051 --> 31:12.800
I think the only reason they gave you the position

419
31:12.820 --> 31:15.160
was because the teachers didn’t want to upset Tokyo.

420
31:16.040 --> 31:17.920
Why do you have to rub it in?

421
31:18.326 --> 31:21.440
Yeah, I know I sing off-key.

422
31:21.744 --> 31:23.920
And it was shitty of me to use Tokyo’s name

423
31:23.945 --> 31:25.480
to get myself made the school’s lead singer.

424
31:25.616 --> 31:28.080
But so what? I still worked hard, didn’t I?

425
31:29.275 --> 31:32.440
You know I practiced every single day.

426
31:34.984 --> 31:37.360
Hey, it’s okay, Jai.

427
31:39.118 --> 31:40.800
You could always sing on TikTok.

428
31:41.000 --> 31:42.600
That won’t work.

429
31:44.488 --> 31:46.440
I need the school singer position on my portfolio

430
31:46.489 --> 31:48.180
to apply for a university admissions quota.

431
31:48.712 --> 31:50.580
If they take the position away from me like this,

432
31:51.176 --> 31:53.360
my chances are practically zero.

433
31:54.520 --> 31:57.280
Who’s going to take responsibility for all the work I’ve put in?

434
31:59.422 --> 32:00.880
I’m sure it’ll be okay.

435
32:00.950 --> 32:03.250
We’ll find another way.

436
32:03.610 --> 32:06.440
And if you’re truly determined, you can still get in through the entrance exam.

437
32:08.160 --> 32:11.000
Hey. It’ll be okay.

438
32:21.776 --> 32:23.480
When my braid is on the left,

439
32:24.440 --> 32:25.560
that’s your cue to meet me in the bathroom.

440
32:30.854 --> 32:31.936
And…

441
32:33.176 --> 32:34.520
What about the right side?

442
32:49.180 --> 32:50.181
You need to meet me here.

443
32:57.846 --> 32:58.971
And…

444
32:59.984 --> 33:01.085
What if

445
33:04.627 --> 33:05.880
I want to kiss you like this?

446
33:07.680 --> 33:09.440
There's no secret code for that.

447
33:11.619 --> 33:13.720
If you can't figure it out,

448
33:17.781 --> 33:18.782
then it's your loss.

449
33:26.408 --> 33:27.409
Your loss.

450
33:46.862 --> 33:48.560
Blue.

451
33:53.843 --> 33:55.200
I know you don’t want to talk to me, Blue.

452
33:56.190 --> 33:58.080
But I know the reason you won’t take me back

453
34:01.491 --> 34:02.840
is because you are dating someone, right?

454
34:06.470 --> 34:07.471
It’s Tokyo, isn’t it?

455
34:21.896 --> 34:24.358
Whether it’s true or not, it’s none of your business.

456
34:26.707 --> 34:27.708
No, it isn’t.

457
34:28.275 --> 34:29.920
But aren’t your families enemies?

458
34:31.760 --> 34:33.560
I know you probably don’t care what your father thinks,

459
34:34.659 --> 34:37.010
but I’ve heard Tokyo’s family can be pretty ruthless.

460
34:39.240 --> 34:40.241
Are you threatening me?

461
34:42.370 --> 34:43.371
No.

462
34:43.653 --> 34:44.654
But...

463
34:44.660 --> 34:46.980
if you don’t want me telling your family or Tokyo’s,

464
34:48.120 --> 34:49.521
then give me another chance.

465
35:25.075 --> 35:26.720
♪ Because I’ve never ♪

466
35:26.931 --> 35:30.200
♪ Been good with words ♪

467
35:30.739 --> 35:35.740
♪ You know that better than anyone ♪

468
35:36.299 --> 35:41.280
♪ And the reason I never say ♪

469
35:41.430 --> 35:45.930
♪ The sweet, heartfelt things others do ♪

470
35:45.960 --> 35:49.160
♪ Is because I believe a love song ♪

471
35:49.261 --> 35:51.680
♪ Dedicated to you ♪

472
35:51.835 --> 35:56.920
♪ Should be one song, and one song alone ♪

473
35:57.867 --> 36:00.920
♪ If there were too many ♪

474
36:01.187 --> 36:03.640
♪ All those tender words ♪

475
36:03.688 --> 36:08.989
♪ Might begin to lose their meaning ♪

476
36:09.520 --> 36:11.820
♪ I want you to know ♪

477
36:14.638 --> 36:16.520
Blue, is Tong hitting on you?

478
36:17.086 --> 36:19.280
A new couple in the making. Here we go.

479
36:27.352 --> 36:29.120
Actually, I’m not here to hit on Blue.

480
36:30.993 --> 36:32.300
I’m Blue’s ex.

481
36:33.256 --> 36:34.920
I came here to ask her to take me back.

482
36:36.493 --> 36:39.240
Shit. Is he your favorite ex or something?

483
36:39.368 --> 36:41.200
Well, Blue? What are you gonna do? Tell him.

484
36:43.080 --> 36:44.081
For sure.

485
36:59.115 --> 37:00.280
Let's rehearse again.

486
37:09.984 --> 37:10.985
Here.

487
37:11.640 --> 37:12.880
It’s the cheesecake you like.

488
37:14.680 --> 37:15.681
Thanks.

489
37:18.550 --> 37:19.800
But I don’t like it anymore.

490
37:22.656 --> 37:24.380
Are you still mad at me?

491
37:25.232 --> 37:26.240
I’m sorry.

492
37:26.979 --> 37:29.280
Can we start over?

493
37:30.632 --> 37:32.920
It has nothing to do with you threatening me.

494
37:34.440 --> 37:35.560
But you know that doing all this

495
37:36.112 --> 37:38.400
still won’t make me take you back, right?

496
37:41.056 --> 37:44.160
And I’m not angry that you followed me here.

497
37:46.667 --> 37:48.380
Because I know the school you transferred to

498
37:48.440 --> 37:50.180
really is known for its athletic admissions quota.

499
37:54.368 --> 37:55.369
What I am angry about

500
37:56.910 --> 37:58.380
is that you tried to blackmail me.

501
37:59.440 --> 38:00.780
- Please, Blue-- - Tone.

502
38:01.730 --> 38:04.520
Believe it or not, before all this,

503
38:04.910 --> 38:06.680
I thought that once I went back home,

504
38:07.016 --> 38:09.720
I could still text you and talk to you like before.

505
38:09.774 --> 38:10.775
I thought we could be friends.

506
38:12.300 --> 38:13.301
But now,

507
38:14.174 --> 38:15.480
I don’t want anything to do with you anymore.

508
38:16.378 --> 38:19.360
But I only did it because I wanted to keep you safe.

509
38:20.691 --> 38:22.227
Your mom told me everything

510
38:22.264 --> 38:23.840
about how dangerous that family is.

511
38:25.320 --> 38:27.920
What you and Tokyo are doing really isn’t safe.

512
38:28.957 --> 38:31.800
Tokyo could end up in danger too.

513
38:32.958 --> 38:33.960
Please believe me.

514
38:35.773 --> 38:37.180
Don’t put yourself at risk.

515
38:39.240 --> 38:40.520
I’ll protect you.

516
38:51.803 --> 38:52.804
Sorry.

517
38:54.011 --> 38:55.720
We’re better off staying exes.

518
39:43.160 --> 39:46.440
♪ On a night with no stars in the sky ♪

519
39:46.640 --> 39:49.040
♪ Just another ordinary night ♪

520
39:49.141 --> 39:54.640
♪ Nothing around us is setting the mood ♪

521
39:55.040 --> 39:57.600
♪ I want to reach out and hold your hand ♪

522
39:58.080 --> 39:59.081
What is it?

523
40:02.075 --> 40:03.440
What is going on?

524
40:03.456 --> 40:06.360
Come on, don't be shy. Just look at him.

525
40:06.603 --> 40:08.080
♪ Because I’ve never ♪

526
40:08.204 --> 40:11.480
♪ Been good with words ♪

527
40:11.970 --> 40:16.000
♪ You know that better than anyone ♪

528
40:16.160 --> 40:18.720
Hey, it’s okay.

529
40:18.800 --> 40:20.640
We can always start our own band later.

530
40:21.269 --> 40:22.270
Right?

531
40:23.312 --> 40:24.600
We should be worried about Tokyo instead.

532
40:24.613 --> 40:25.720
Who knows where the hell she went?

533
40:27.360 --> 40:28.720
She was so shocked that she just disappeared.

534
40:33.278 --> 40:38.180
♪ Should be one song, and one song alone ♪

535
40:39.280 --> 40:41.920
♪ If there were too many ♪

536
40:42.400 --> 40:44.720
♪ All those tender words ♪

537
40:45.222 --> 40:49.440
♪ Might begin to lose their meaning ♪

538
40:50.560 --> 40:52.561
♪ I want you to know ♪

539
40:53.240 --> 40:56.600
♪ Let our eyes do the talking ♪

540
40:57.440 --> 40:59.640
♪ Every time our gazes meet ♪

541
41:00.245 --> 41:01.246
Ouch!

542
41:02.958 --> 41:03.959
Ow!

543
41:04.800 --> 41:05.801
Let me go!

544
41:07.000 --> 41:08.001
Who are you?

545
41:14.440 --> 41:15.441
Tokyo?

546
41:23.283 --> 41:25.000
You didn’t show up that day

547
41:25.848 --> 41:28.180
because you were afraid someone would see us together, right?

548
41:29.139 --> 41:30.880
If it was because Tong threatened you like that,

549
41:31.421 --> 41:32.640
I’ve already talked to Tong and sorted it out.

550
41:40.694 --> 41:41.695
Can I give you a hand?

551
41:45.200 --> 41:46.920
It's okay. I can do this.

552
41:48.091 --> 41:49.320
I’ve already asked Blue to take me back.

553
41:52.659 --> 41:53.720
The reason I moved here

554
41:53.760 --> 41:55.261
is because Blue’s mother asked me to.

555
41:57.780 --> 42:00.000
She wants Blue and me to get back together.

556
42:01.560 --> 42:02.840
Let me ask you something.

557
42:03.795 --> 42:06.330
What exactly are you to Blue?

558
42:07.683 --> 42:08.760
Whatever I am,

559
42:09.582 --> 42:11.083
I’m more than an ex like you.

560
42:13.254 --> 42:14.720
You do realize that you’re just

561
42:14.917 --> 42:16.120
dragging Blue into

562
42:16.218 --> 42:17.480
the feud between our families, don’t you?

563
42:18.603 --> 42:20.120
You’re making things difficult for her.

564
42:21.046 --> 42:22.440
If you truly care about Blue,

565
42:23.247 --> 42:24.360
then let her go.

566
42:40.232 --> 42:42.180
If that’s your idea of threatening me,

567
42:42.856 --> 42:44.000
you need to try harder.

568
42:44.955 --> 42:46.000
You know

569
42:46.784 --> 42:48.560
I was raised in a mafia family.

570
42:49.664 --> 42:51.080
Something like this won’t scare me.

571
42:52.200 --> 42:54.960
And stop using the adults’ feud as an excuse.

572
42:56.240 --> 42:57.880
We can handle

573
42:58.360 --> 42:59.600
our own relationships.

574
43:00.979 --> 43:01.980
We don’t need you interfering.

575
43:26.334 --> 43:27.920
But none of that matters now.

576
43:30.491 --> 43:31.492
I...

577
43:31.920 --> 43:34.200
I really don’t need you to do anything for me.

578
43:37.627 --> 43:41.160
And I don’t want the adults involved in anything between us,

579
43:42.720 --> 43:43.721
whether it’s school

580
43:44.680 --> 43:45.840
or our relationship.

581
43:51.580 --> 43:52.581
I...

582
43:53.355 --> 43:55.640
I don’t have any grand dreams like you,

583
43:57.400 --> 43:58.401
like Jai,

584
43:59.518 --> 44:01.120
or like our other friends.

585
44:04.944 --> 44:06.380
I just know

586
44:08.240 --> 44:09.520
that I want to be with you.

587
44:10.841 --> 44:12.280
And I want the freedom

588
44:13.157 --> 44:14.440
to make my own choices.

589
44:16.080 --> 44:17.081
That’s all.

590
44:22.139 --> 44:24.720
We’re not going to break up

591
44:27.093 --> 44:28.094
because of anyone else.

592
44:30.102 --> 44:31.360
If we ever do break up,

593
44:34.059 --> 44:35.880
it should be because we don’t love each other anymore.

594
44:37.816 --> 44:38.817
Okay?

595
45:00.432 --> 45:01.920
♪ To you ♪

596
45:04.160 --> 45:06.200
♪ The one who means everything to me ♪

597
45:08.464 --> 45:12.400
♪ I'll be waiting to walk beside you ♪

598
45:14.224 --> 45:16.840
♪ Our dreams won't be far away ♪

599
45:18.006 --> 45:19.160
♪ But you ♪

600
45:21.611 --> 45:25.480
♪ slowly faded away and changed ♪

601
45:26.040 --> 45:29.640
♪ My journey toward my dreams came to an end ♪

602
45:31.689 --> 45:34.400
♪ No matter how long it takes ♪

603
45:35.437 --> 45:38.800
♪ I keep waiting ♪

604
45:40.203 --> 45:41.880
♪ I’ll be waiting ♪

605
45:42.539 --> 45:45.160
♪ Though it may be only a dream ♪

606
45:45.878 --> 45:49.879
♪ Of a better day ♪

607
45:51.160 --> 45:53.720
♪ When you return to me ♪

608
45:54.161 --> 45:58.320
♪ There’ll be love and everything we need ♪

609
45:58.619 --> 46:02.480
♪ There’ll be dreams at the end of the road ♪

610
46:02.620 --> 46:07.000
♪ There'll be the two of us, walking side by side ♪

611
46:10.435 --> 46:11.520
♪ To you ♪

612
46:11.832 --> 46:15.520
♪ Who give love depth ♪

613
46:16.120 --> 46:20.240
♪ Who’ll lead me to where I belong ♪

614
46:20.630 --> 46:24.560
♪ There’ll be love and everything we need ♪

615
46:27.824 --> 46:29.280
♪ To you ♪

616
46:29.328 --> 46:33.360
♪ There’ll be love and everything we need ♪

617
